### The SU(2) group-theory arithmetic is settled

`(11/24)·C_A` with `C_A(SU(2)) = 2` is exactly `11/12`, so once the four joint
orbit sums of the *same literal* Wilson + reduced Faddeev–Popov + Haar
evaluator are enclosed in `[−1/2, 1/2]`,

    β_Z ≥ 11/12 − 1/2 = 5/12 > 0.

Proved in
